      "evidenceText": "Mirrored bar chart from CSV How to use: drop a .csv file onto the box below (or paste CSV text into it), then press Draw chart . date,total,Series A,Series B,note 2026-01-12,310,46,120, 2026-01-13,480,96,250,\"This is an annotation\" One header row, then one row per day. Columns in this order: date : day in YYYY-MM-DD format. Dates must be unique and in ascending order (gaps are allowed). total : the grey bar, drawn identically above and below the axis. 3rd column : the coloured overlay on the top half. Its header text becomes the label (e.g. Series A ). 4th column : the coloured overlay on the bottom half. Its header text becomes the label (e.g. Series B ). note (optional 5th column) : text to annotate that day's bar. Leave empty for no note. Wrap text containing commas in double quotes. Values must be numbers ≥ 0, and neither overlay can be larger than total . Inspired by Sebastian Gräff at The European Correspondent: Rioting for a reason . View the code on GitHub Draw chart Load sample data Download sample CSV",
